(function(E){ const x = E["exam-07"] = E["exam-07"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x07-l2"] = {"id":"x07-l2","patterns":["L2-tours","PARA-place"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 2: a site visit with a map","tr":"Listening Part 2: haritalı bir alan ziyareti","fa":"Listening Part 2: بازدید از یک محوطه با نقشه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to answer A-C questions about a talk when the obvious answer is corrected, and to label a map by following the speaker’s route from the entrance.","tr":"Bu derste akla gelen cevabın düzeltildiği bir konuşma hakkındaki A-C sorularını cevaplamayı ve konuşmacının girişten başlayan güzergâhını izleyerek bir haritayı etiketlemeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری به سؤال‌های A-C درباره‌ی صحبتی جواب بدهی که در آن جواب بدیهی اصلاح می‌شود، و با دنبال کردن مسیر گوینده از ورودی، روی یک نقشه برچسب بگذاری."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 2: a site visit with a map","tr":"Listening Part 2: haritalı bir alan ziyareti","fa":"Listening Part 2: بازدید از یک محوطه با نقشه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to answer A-C questions about a talk when the obvious answer is corrected, and to label a map by following the speaker’s route from the entrance.","tr":"Bu derste akla gelen cevabın düzeltildiği bir konuşma hakkındaki A-C sorularını cevaplamayı ve konuşmacının girişten başlayan güzergâhını izleyerek bir haritayı etiketlemeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری به سؤال‌های A-C درباره‌ی صحبتی جواب بدهی که در آن جواب بدیهی اصلاح می‌شود، و با دنبال کردن مسیر گوینده از ورودی، روی یک نقشه برچسب بگذاری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"1"},{"label":{"en":"Letters on the map","tr":"Haritadaki harf","fa":"حرف‌های روی نقشه"},"value":"A-G"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a Roman villa dig","tr":"Bu sınav: bir Roma villası kazısı","fa":"این آزمون: کاوش در یک ویلای رومی"},"intro":{"en":"Tours and visitor talks are the most common Part 2 situation, and many of them end with a map or plan. The speaker usually gives information first and then describes the site from the entrance.","tr":"Turlar ve ziyaretçi konuşmaları en sık çıkan Part 2 durumudur ve birçoğu bir harita ya da planla biter. Konuşmacı genelde önce bilgi verir, sonra alanı girişten başlayarak anlatır.","fa":"تورها و صحبت برای بازدیدکننده‌ها رایج‌ترین موقعیت Part 2 هستند و خیلی‌هایشان با یک نقشه یا پلان تمام می‌شوند. گوینده معمولاً اول اطلاعات می‌دهد و بعد محوطه را از ورودی توصیف می‌کند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x07-l2-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L2-tours","PARA-place"],"often":{"pattern":"L2-tours","n":13,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 13 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 13’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۳ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A guided visit to a historic site","tr":"Tarihî bir alana rehberli ziyaret","fa":"بازدید راهنماشده از یک محوطه‌ی تاریخی"},"asks":{"en":"An expert welcomes a group: how the site was found, the aim of the project, who takes part, an important find and practical points. Then she explains where things are on a map of the site.","tr":"Bir uzman bir grubu karşılıyor: alanın nasıl bulunduğu, projenin amacı, kimlerin katıldığı, önemli bir buluntu ve pratik noktalar. Sonra alanın haritasında her şeyin nerede olduğunu anlatıyor.","fa":"یک کارشناس از یک گروه استقبال می‌کند: محوطه چطور پیدا شد، هدف پروژه، چه کسانی شرکت دارند، یک یافته‌ی مهم و نکته‌های عملی. بعد توضیح می‌دهد هر چیز روی نقشه‌ی محوطه کجاست."},"fields":["How it was found","This year’s aim","The volunteers","The key find","What to bring","Where finds go","Places on the map"],"words":[{"a":"came to light","b":"was discovered / was found","tr":"gün yüzüne çıktı","fa":"پیدا شد، آشکار شد"},{"a":"aim","b":"what we want to find out / the purpose","tr":"amaç","fa":"هدف"},{"a":"abandoned","b":"left empty / people moved away","tr":"terk edildi","fa":"رها شد"},{"a":"excavate","b":"dig carefully to find old objects","tr":"kazı yapmak","fa":"حفاری کردن"},{"a":"a trench","b":"a long, narrow hole dug in the ground","tr":"hendek","fa":"ترانشه، گودالی دراز و باریک"},{"a":"we provide","b":"you don’t need to bring","tr":"biz sağlıyoruz","fa":"ما فراهم می‌کنیم"},{"a":"on display","b":"shown to the public","tr":"sergileniyor","fa":"در معرض نمایش"},{"a":"on your left","b":"to the left as you walk up","tr":"solunda","fa":"سمت چپت"},{"a":"behind","b":"at the back of / further from you","tr":"arkasında","fa":"پشتِ"},{"a":"on the far side of","b":"beyond / on the other side of","tr":"... öbür tarafında","fa":"آن طرفِ"},{"a":"opposite","b":"facing / across the path from","tr":"karşısında","fa":"روبه‌روی"},{"a":"just before you reach","b":"immediately before","tr":"... varmadan hemen önce","fa":"درست قبل از رسیدن به"}],"traps":[{"en":"MCQ: the expected answer is mentioned first and then corrected: \"People assume... In fact...\" Wait for the correction.","tr":"Çoktan seçmeli: beklenen cevap önce söylenir, sonra düzeltilir: \"İnsanlar sanıyor ki... Aslında...\" Düzeltmeyi bekle.","fa":"چندگزینه‌ای: جواب قابل انتظار اول گفته و بعد اصلاح می‌شود: «مردم فکر می‌کنند... در واقع...». منتظر اصلاح بمان."},{"en":"Map: follow the speaker’s route from the starting point. Left and right depend on the direction you are facing, usually from the entrance.","tr":"Harita: konuşmacının güzergâhını başlangıç noktasından takip et. Sol ve sağ, genelde girişten baktığın yöne göre değişir.","fa":"نقشه: مسیر گوینده را از نقطه‌ی شروع دنبال کن. چپ و راست به جهتی بستگی دارد که رو به آن ایستاده‌ای، معمولاً از ورودی."},{"en":"A place that has moved or a past use: \"We used to send everything to...\" Mark the place that is true now.","tr":"Yer değiştirmiş bir şey ya da eski bir kullanım: \"Eskiden her şeyi ...’e gönderirdik\" Şu an doğru olanı işaretle.","fa":"جایی که عوض شده یا کاربری قدیمی: «قبلاً همه‌چیز را به ... می‌فرستادیم». جایی را علامت بزن که الان درست است."}],"example":{"lines":[["Guide","From the gate, walk straight ahead. The café is the first building on your right, just past the fountain."]],"item":"Map: Café = A (left of the path, before the fountain) or B (right of the path, after the fountain)?","answer":"B","why":{"en":"\"On your right\" and \"just past the fountain\" both point to B.","tr":"\"Sağında\" ve \"çeşmeyi geçince hemen\" ikisi de B’yi gösteriyor.","fa":"«سمت راستت» و «درست بعد از فواره» هر دو B را نشان می‌دهند."}}},{"id":"L2-map-heritage","ctx":["L2-map-heritage","L2-tours"],"title":{"en":"Heritage and visitor sites","tr":"Tarihî yerler ve ziyaretçi alanları","fa":"مکان‌های تاریخی و بازدیدی"},"asks":{"en":"A guide shows visitors round a castle, a mill, an old house or an archaeology site. You label rooms or areas such as the ticket office, the shop, the old kitchens, an exhibition or a viewing platform.","tr":"Bir rehber ziyaretçileri bir kalede, bir değirmende, eski bir evde ya da bir kazı alanında gezdirir. Bilet gişesi, dükkân, eski mutfaklar, bir sergi ya da seyir terası gibi odaları veya alanları etiketlersin.","fa":"یک راهنما بازدیدکننده‌ها را در یک قلعه، یک آسیاب، یک خانه‌ی قدیمی یا یک محوطه‌ی باستانی می‌گرداند. اتاق‌ها یا جاهایی مثل باجه‌ی بلیت، فروشگاه، آشپزخانه‌های قدیمی، نمایشگاه یا سکوی تماشا را برچسب می‌زنی."},"fields":["Ticket office","Gift shop","Exhibition room","Old kitchens","Viewing platform","Excavation site","Gardens"],"words":[{"a":"ground floor","b":"downstairs / at street level","tr":"zemin kat","fa":"طبقه‌ی همکف"},{"a":"courtyard","b":"the open square in the middle","tr":"avlu","fa":"حیاط"},{"a":"tower","b":"the tall round building","tr":"kule","fa":"برج"},{"a":"exhibition","b":"the display room","tr":"sergi","fa":"نمایشگاه"},{"a":"walls","b":"the old stone walls round the site","tr":"surlar","fa":"دیوارهای قدیمی"},{"a":"gate","b":"the way in through the walls","tr":"kapı","fa":"دروازه"},{"a":"excavation","b":"where they are digging","tr":"kazı alanı","fa":"محل کاوش"},{"a":"wing","b":"the east side of the house","tr":"kanat","fa":"بال ساختمان"},{"a":"straight ahead","b":"in front of you as you walk","tr":"dümdüz ileride","fa":"درست جلوی رو"},{"a":"to the left of","b":"on its left side","tr":"... -in solunda","fa":"سمت چپِ"},{"a":"just inside","b":"as soon as you go through","tr":"hemen içeride","fa":"درست بعد از ورود"},{"a":"between","b":"with one on each side","tr":"arasında","fa":"بین"}],"traps":[{"en":"Rooms on two floors: the plan shows one floor, so ignore what is \"upstairs\".","tr":"İki katlı odalar: plan tek katı gösterir; \"üst kattakileri\" boş ver.","fa":"اتاق‌ها در دو طبقه: پلان فقط یک طبقه را نشان می‌دهد، پس چیزهای «طبقه‌ی بالا» را نادیده بگیر."},{"en":"\"Opposite the shop\" and \"next to the shop\" are different letters. Check the side.","tr":"\"Dükkânın karşısında\" ile \"dükkânın yanında\" farklı harflerdir. Hangi tarafta olduğuna bak.","fa":"«روبه‌روی فروشگاه» و «کنار فروشگاه» دو حرف متفاوت‌اند. سمتش را چک کن."}],"example":{"lines":[["Guide","Once you’re through the main gate, the courtyard is straight ahead."],["Guide","The shop is just inside the gate on your right."],["Guide","And the cafe is opposite it, on the left."]],"item":"Cafe: ___   (plan: gate at the bottom, courtyard in the middle; A just inside the gate on the right, B just inside the gate on the left, C beyond the courtyard)","answer":"B","why":{"en":"The shop is A. \"Opposite it, on the left\" is B.","tr":"Dükkân A. \"Opposite it, on the left\" B’dir.","fa":"فروشگاه A است. «Opposite it, on the left» یعنی B."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L2-tours"],"often":{"pattern":"L2-tours","n":13,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 13 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 13’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۳ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Six A-C questions, then a map","tr":"Altı A-C sorusu, sonra bir harita","fa":"شش سؤال A-C، بعد یک نقشه"},"body":{"en":"Questions 11-16: choose A, B or C. Questions 17-20: label a map with letters A-G; there are more letters than questions, and each letter is used once at most. You read Questions 17-20 in the break, so use that time to find the entrance and the paths.","tr":"Soru 11-16: A, B ya da C’yi seç. Soru 17-20: bir haritayı A-G harfleriyle etiketle; harf sayısı soru sayısından fazla ve her harf en fazla bir kez kullanılır. Soru 17-20’yi molada okursun; bu zamanı girişi ve yolları bulmak için kullan.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۱ تا ۱۶: A، B یا C را انتخاب کن. سؤال‌های ۱۷ تا ۲۰: روی نقشه با حرف‌های A تا G برچسب بگذار؛ حرف‌ها از سؤال‌ها بیشترند و هر حرف حداکثر یک بار به کار می‌رود. سؤال‌های ۱۷ تا ۲۰ را در وقفه می‌خوانی، پس از آن وقت برای پیدا کردن ورودی و مسیرها استفاده کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Follow the route","tr":"Güzergâhı takip et","fa":"مسیر را دنبال کن"},"steps":[{"en":"In the break, find the starting point on the map and the names already printed: gate, path, car park.","tr":"Molada haritada başlangıç noktasını ve zaten yazılı isimleri bul: kapı, yol, otopark.","fa":"در وقفه نقطه‌ی شروع و اسم‌های چاپ‌شده روی نقشه را پیدا کن: در، مسیر، پارکینگ."},{"en":"Put your pencil on the starting point and move it as the speaker moves: walk up, carry on, at the top.","tr":"Kalemini başlangıç noktasına koy ve konuşan ilerledikçe onu hareket ettir: walk up, carry on, at the top.","fa":"مدادت را روی نقطه‌ی شروع بگذار و همراه گوینده حرکتش بده: walk up، carry on، at the top."},{"en":"Listen for the position words: on your left, behind, on the far side, opposite, just before.","tr":"Konum kelimelerini dinle: on your left, behind, on the far side, opposite, just before.","fa":"به کلمه‌های موقعیت گوش بده: on your left، behind، on the far side، opposite، just before."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"What people expect","tr":"İnsanların beklediği","fa":"چیزی که مردم انتظار دارند"},"body":{"en":"In the first half, the speaker often names the answer you would guess and then corrects it: \"People often assume... In fact...\" or \"You might expect... But actually...\". Choose the option that follows the correction.","tr":"İlk yarıda konuşan çoğu zaman tahmin edeceğin cevabı söyler, sonra düzeltir: \"İnsanlar çoğu zaman sanır ki... Aslında...\" ya da \"... bekleyebilirsiniz. Ama aslında...\". Düzeltmeden sonra gelen seçeneği seç.","fa":"در نیمه‌ی اول، گوینده اغلب جوابی را که حدس می‌زنی می‌گوید و بعد اصلاحش می‌کند: «مردم اغلب فکر می‌کنند... در واقع...» یا «شاید انتظار داشته باشی... اما در واقع...». گزینه‌ای را انتخاب کن که بعد از اصلاح می‌آید."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One map label, step by step","tr":"Bir harita etiketi, adım adım","fa":"یک برچسب نقشه، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Label the map. Write the correct letter.","item":"Picnic area: A (left of the gate) · B (top left, beside the lake) · C (top right, beside the lake)","lines":[["Guide","From the gate, follow the path up to the lake. The picnic area is at the top, on the right-hand side of the lake."]],"answer":"C","walk":[{"en":"Start at the gate and move up the path with your pencil.","tr":"Kapıdan başla ve kalemini yol boyunca yukarı hareket ettir.","fa":"از در شروع کن و مدادت را در مسیر بالا ببر."},{"en":"\"At the top\" rules out A.","tr":"\"Yukarıda\" A’yı eler.","fa":"«بالا» A را رد می‌کند."},{"en":"\"On the right-hand side of the lake\" = C, not B.","tr":"\"Gölün sağ tarafında\" = C, B değil.","fa":"«سمت راست دریاچه» یعنی C، نه B."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"\"You might think the old bridge was built for trains. Actually, it was built to carry water to the town.\" What was the bridge built for?","options":["to carry trains","to carry cars","to carry water to the town"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Trains are what you might think; \"actually\" gives the answer: water for the town.","tr":"Trenler senin düşünebileceğin şey; \"actually\" cevabı veriyor: kasabaya su.","fa":"قطار چیزی است که شاید فکر کنی؛ «actually» جواب را می‌دهد: آب برای شهر."}},"remember":{"en":"Wait for the correction in the first half, and follow the route with your pencil on the map.","tr":"İlk yarıda düzeltmeyi bekle ve haritada güzergâhı kalemle takip et.","fa":"در نیمه‌ی اول منتظر اصلاح بمان و روی نقشه مسیر را با مداد دنبال کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x07-l2-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-l2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 2","title":{"en":"The Hatherley Roman Villa dig","tr":"Hatherley Roma Villası kazısı","fa":"کاوش ویلای رومی هاترلی"},"timed":7,"ctx":["L2-tours"],"script":[{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"Good morning, everyone, and welcome to the Hatherley Roman Villa community dig. I'm Fiona Kerr, and I'm the archaeologist in charge of the site this summer. Before you start work, I'd like to tell you a little about the villa and the project, and then I'll show you around the site."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"People often assume that the villa was found by a farmer ploughing his field, because that's how many Roman sites come to light. In fact, nobody had any idea it was here until the very dry summer of 1976, when a pilot flying over the valley noticed dark lines in the yellow grass. Those lines were the walls of the villa, showing through the soil, and his photographs are still in the county archive."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"Since then, there have been several digs here, but this one has a particular aim. We already know roughly how big the villa was, and we've found the bath house, so that isn't what we're looking for. What we want to find out this year is when the villa was finally abandoned. Was it suddenly, or did the family slowly move away? The answer will tell us a lot about what was happening in the region at the end of the Roman period."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"I should say a word about who you'll be working with. You might expect a dig like this to be full of archaeology students, and we do have a few. But more than half of our volunteers are retired people from the villages nearby, many of whom have been coming back every summer for ten years or more. They know the site better than I do."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"Last season produced some wonderful finds. Visitors always get excited about the mosaic floor we uncovered in the main room, and it is beautiful. But the find that really changed our thinking was a tiny bronze coin, found under a collapsed wall. It was made much later than we expected, which suggests that people were still living here long after we thought the villa had been abandoned."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"Now, a few practical points. We provide all the tools, including trowels and buckets, and we have gloves in every size. What we do recommend you bring is a pair of knee pads, because you'll spend most of the day kneeling on hard ground. And please bring plenty of water and a hat."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"Anything you find is recorded, washed and labelled on site. We used to send everything straight to the university laboratory, but these days the best finds stay in the valley for a while. At the end of the season they'll be on display in the village hall for two weeks, so that local people can see what's been found on their doorstep."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"Right, let me tell you where everything is. Have a look at the map I've given you. We're standing at the entrance gate, at the bottom of the map. The car park is on your left as you face the site."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"If you walk up the path from the gate, the first thing you'll come to, on your left, is the toilet block. It's right behind the car park, so you can't miss it."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"Carry on up the path and you'll reach the main trench, which is the large rectangle in the middle of the site. That's where most of you will be working. The finds tent is on the far side of the trench, to the right, just above the stream. That's where you'll take anything you dig up, and where the washing is done."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"For visitors who want to watch without getting in the way, we've built a viewing platform. It's at the top of the map, behind the trench, between the woodland and the corner of the field. It gives a really good view of the whole villa."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"And finally, the tool store. That's the small shed on the right of the path, just before you reach the trench, opposite the toilets. Please put everything back there at the end of the day."},{"who":"Archaeologist","line":"OK, if you'd all like to follow me up the path, we'll start with a quick look at the trench."}],"map":{"title":"Hatherley Roman Villa: site plan","orientation":"north at the top","coords":"0-100 from the top-left corner","features":[{"label":"Woodland","type":"trees","box":[25,0,25,25]},{"label":"Field","type":"field","box":[75,0,25,25]},{"label":"Main trench","type":"area","box":[25,25,50,25]},{"label":"Path","type":"path","from":[37,95],"to":[37,50]},{"label":"Stream","type":"water","from":[75,62],"to":[100,62]},{"label":"Car park","type":"parking","box":[0,75,25,25]},{"label":"Entrance gate","type":"gate","at":[37,97]},{"label":"Farm track","type":"road","from":[75,88],"to":[100,88]}],"letters":[{"l":"A","at":[12,12]},{"l":"B","at":[62,12]},{"l":"C","at":[12,37]},{"l":"D","at":[62,88]},{"l":"E","at":[88,37]},{"l":"F","at":[12,62]},{"l":"G","at":[62,62]}]},"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 11-16. Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":11,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"How was the villa first discovered?","options":["A A farmer found walls while ploughing.","B Builders found it while digging.","C Lines in dry grass were seen from the air."],"correct":2,"evidence":"a pilot flying over the valley noticed dark lines in the yellow grass","why":{"en":"Ploughing is what \"people often assume\". \"In fact... a pilot... noticed dark lines in the yellow grass.\"","tr":"Sürmek \"insanların çoğu zaman sandığı\" şey. \"Aslında... bir pilot... sarı çimlerde koyu çizgiler fark etti.\"","fa":"شخم زدن چیزی است که «مردم اغلب فکر می‌کنند». «در واقع... یک خلبان... خط‌های تیره‌ای در علف‌های زرد دید»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What is the main aim of this year’s dig?","options":["A to discover when people stopped living in the villa","B to find the bath house","C to measure the size of the villa"],"correct":0,"evidence":"What we want to find out this year is when the villa was finally abandoned","why":{"en":"The size is \"roughly\" known and the bath house has been found. The aim is \"when the villa was finally abandoned\".","tr":"Büyüklüğü \"kabaca\" biliniyor ve hamam bulundu. Amaç \"villanın en sonunda ne zaman terk edildiği\".","fa":"اندازه «تقریباً» معلوم است و حمام پیدا شده. هدف این است که «ویلا بالاخره کی رها شد»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]},{"n":13,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Who are most of the volunteers?","options":["A archaeology students","B retired local people","C families from the city"],"correct":1,"evidence":"more than half of our volunteers are retired people from the villages nearby","why":{"en":"Students are what \"you might expect\", and there are \"a few\". \"More than half... are retired people from the villages nearby.\"","tr":"Öğrenciler \"bekleyebileceğin\" şey ve \"birkaç tane\" var. \"Yarıdan fazlası... yakındaki köylerden emekliler.\"","fa":"دانشجوها چیزی‌اند که «شاید انتظار داشته باشی» و «چند نفری» هستند. «بیش از نیمی... بازنشسته‌های روستاهای نزدیک‌اند»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":14,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which find from last season was the most important?","options":["A a mosaic floor","B a small coin","C a collapsed wall"],"correct":1,"evidence":"the find that really changed our thinking was a tiny bronze coin","why":{"en":"Visitors get excited about the mosaic, but \"the find that really changed our thinking was a tiny bronze coin\".","tr":"Ziyaretçiler mozaiğe heyecanlanıyor ama \"düşüncemizi gerçekten değiştiren buluntu küçük bir bronz sikkeydi\".","fa":"بازدیدکننده‌ها برای موزاییک هیجان‌زده می‌شوند، اما «یافته‌ای که واقعاً نظرمان را عوض کرد یک سکه‌ی کوچک برنزی بود»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]},{"n":15,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What are volunteers advised to bring?","options":["A knee pads","B their own trowel","C gloves"],"correct":0,"evidence":"What we do recommend you bring is a pair of knee pads","why":{"en":"Trowels and gloves are provided. \"What we do recommend you bring is a pair of knee pads.\"","tr":"Mala ve eldiven sağlanıyor. \"Getirmenizi önerdiğimiz şey bir çift dizlik.\"","fa":"ماله و دستکش فراهم است. «چیزی که توصیه می‌کنیم بیاورید یک جفت زانوبند است»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]},{"n":16,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What will happen to the best finds at the end of the season?","options":["A They will go straight to a university.","B They will be sold to a museum.","C The village hall will exhibit them."],"correct":2,"evidence":"they'll be on display in the village hall for two weeks","why":{"en":"Sending everything to the university is what they \"used to\" do. Now the finds will be \"on display in the village hall\".","tr":"Her şeyi üniversiteye göndermek \"eskiden\" yaptıkları şeydi. Artık buluntular \"köy salonunda sergilenecek\".","fa":"فرستادن همه‌چیز به دانشگاه کاری است که «قبلاً» می‌کردند. حالا یافته‌ها «در سالن روستا به نمایش گذاشته می‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 17-20. Label the map below. Write the correct letter, A-G, next to Questions 17-20.","qtype":"map","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"questions":[{"n":17,"kind":"match","prompt":"Toilet block","correct":5,"evidence":"the first thing you'll come to, on your left, is the toilet block","why":{"en":"First on the left up the path, \"right behind the car park\": F.","tr":"Yolda soldaki ilk şey, \"otoparkın hemen arkasında\": F.","fa":"اولین چیز سمت چپ مسیر، «درست پشت پارکینگ»: F."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":18,"kind":"match","prompt":"Finds tent","correct":4,"evidence":"The finds tent is on the far side of the trench, to the right, just above the stream","why":{"en":"\"On the far side of the trench, to the right, just above the stream\": E.","tr":"\"Hendeğin öbür tarafında, sağda, derenin hemen üstünde\": E.","fa":"«آن طرف ترانشه، سمت راست، درست بالای نهر»: E."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":19,"kind":"match","prompt":"Viewing platform","correct":1,"evidence":"between the woodland and the corner of the field","why":{"en":"\"At the top of the map, behind the trench, between the woodland and the corner of the field\": B.","tr":"\"Haritanın üstünde, hendeğin arkasında, koruluk ile tarlanın köşesi arasında\": B.","fa":"«بالای نقشه، پشت ترانشه، بین جنگل و گوشه‌ی مزرعه»: B."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":20,"kind":"match","prompt":"Tool store","correct":6,"evidence":"the small shed on the right of the path, just before you reach the trench, opposite the toilets","why":{"en":"\"On the right of the path, just before you reach the trench, opposite the toilets\": G.","tr":"\"Yolun sağında, hendeğe varmadan hemen önce, tuvaletlerin karşısında\": G.","fa":"«سمت راست مسیر، درست قبل از رسیدن به ترانشه، روبه‌روی توالت‌ها»: G."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]}],"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Archaeologist":{"accent":"Scottish","gender":"F","tts":{"engine":"piper","voice":"en_GB-alba-medium"},"role":"Archaeologist leading the dig"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 2. You will hear an archaeologist talking to volunteers at the start of a community dig. First, you have some time to look at Questions 11 to 16."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 11-16"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 11 to 16."},{"type":"sfx","note":"outdoors: light wind, birds, distant tractor"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":6},{"type":"announcer","text":"Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at Questions 17 to 20."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 17-20"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen and answer Questions 17 to 20."},{"type":"lines","from":7,"to":12},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 2. You now have half a minute to check your answers.","after":30}]},"id":"c-x07-l2-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-l2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The villa was abandoned in the fifth century.\" Abandoned means...","options":["built","left by the people who lived there","repaired"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Abandoned = left empty, no longer used.","tr":"Abandoned = boş bırakılmış, artık kullanılmayan.","fa":"abandoned یعنی خالی رها شده و دیگر استفاده نمی‌شود."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"A speaker says \"on the far side of the lake\". On a map, this means...","options":["on the other side of the lake from you","next to you","in the middle of the lake"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The far side is the side further away from where you are standing.","tr":"Far side, durduğun yerden daha uzak olan taraftır.","fa":"far side یعنی سمتی که از جای تو دورتر است."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Map labelling: the speaker says \"As you come in through the gate, it’s on your left.\" What should you do first?","options":["Look at the top of the map","Choose the letter nearest the middle","Find the gate and face into the map from it"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Left and right are from the entrance, facing into the site.","tr":"Sol ve sağ, girişten alana bakarken belirlenir.","fa":"چپ و راست از ورودی و رو به داخل محوطه تعیین می‌شود."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"Most people think the castle was destroyed in a war. In fact, it was simply taken apart for its stone.\" What happened to the castle?","options":["It was destroyed in a war.","Its stone was taken for building.","It fell down in a storm."],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The war is what most people think; \"in fact\" gives the real answer.","tr":"Savaş çoğu insanın düşündüğü şey; \"in fact\" gerçek cevabı veriyor.","fa":"جنگ چیزی است که بیشتر مردم فکر می‌کنند؛ «in fact» جواب واقعی را می‌دهد."}}],"id":"c-x07-l2-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-l2"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
